# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
/target_cpu
/target_cuda
dist/
__pycache__/
.vscode

# The extension module is BUILD output: `maturin develop` writes a `.so` tagged
# with the platform AND the interpreter (cpython-312-x86_64-linux-gnu), so a
# tracked one is one machine's binary shipped to everyone else — and every
# rebuild is a 42 MB diff. Build it locally; it is never source.
python/gras/*.so
python/gras/*.pyd

# ── Vendored libtorch, datasets and saved models ────────────────────────────
/libtorch
*.safetensors*
/data
assets/
/saved
saved/

# ── Run output and scratch dirs ─────────────────────────────────────────────
results/
logs/
trash/
/examples/*/run/
/benches/*/run/
proptest-regressions/

# ── Profiling intermediates (written to cwd by cargo flamegraph / benches) ──
/flamegraph.svg
/perf.data
/perf.data.old
/dhat-heap.json

# ── Local-only docs and agent context ───────────────────────────────────────
# Tracked docs describe the code; this is the local shelf around it. `/notes/`
# holds the explainers, design plans and measurements, indexed by
# `notes/README.md`. Ignore rules never affect an already-tracked file.
/notes/
AGENTS.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
CONVENTIONS.md
TODO.md
DONE.md
GEMINI.md
NOTES.md
NAS_GUIDE.md
WORKFLOW.md
PROD_REFACTOR_WINS.md
RACE_REVAMP.md
.agents/
.serena/

# ── Local scratch files and stale run dirs ──────────────────────────────────
Makefile
kaggle_guide.rs
kaggle_ev_s6e9.rs
examples/main.rs
1789787353879/
1789503022765/

# ── Only the canonical examples are tracked ─────────────────────────────────
# Anything else under examples/ is a local scratch checkout — the
# bridge/smart-buildings/kagiculture examples moved to the sibling
# `kaggle_exper` repo. The re-includes keep the tracked examples visible to
# `git status`, so they must stay AFTER `/examples/*`.
/examples/*
!/examples/cartpole/
!/examples/cartpole.rs
!/examples/mnist.rs
!/examples/python/
